Body:
Worked through Groq model support in OpenCode and pushed the current implementation locally. Here is a concise status update plus the key code/config snippets.

What changed
- Added provider-agnostic runtime policy fields on models: `systemPrompt`, `disableLocalTools`, `maxActiveTools`, `toolPriority`
- Moved Groq behavior out of session/provider branching and into policy/override data
- Added bundled provider overrides so unusable Groq models can be hidden or adjusted without hardcoding session logic
- Added a Groq-specific system prompt profile
- Made models with `tool_call: false` automatically skip local tool payloads

What now works reliably here
- `groq/compound`
- `groq/compound-mini`
- `groq/meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct`
- `groq/meta-llama/llama-guard-4-12b`
- `groq/moonshotai/kimi-k2-instruct-0905`
- `groq/openai/gpt-oss-120b`
- `groq/openai/gpt-oss-20b`
- `groq/qwen/qwen3-32b`

Models filtered out for now
- `groq/meta-llama/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct` (not accessible on this account)
- `groq/llama-3.1-8b-instant` (bad tool-call behavior)
- `groq/llama-3.3-70b-versatile` (quota/behavior problems here)
- `groq/qwen3-32b` (alias was flaky vs `qwen/qwen3-32b`)

Key snippets

1) Runtime policy data
```ts
